00:27:51.540 --> 00:27:55.820
If you stick around for the post show, we're going to go over the trends of the 2010s and

00:27:55.820 --> 00:28:00.460
stuff like that. But I think now would be a great time to actually talk about Ikari Warriors 2.

00:28:03.720 --> 00:28:08.740
We are going to talk about a vertical run and gun game where you have to destroy the enemy

00:28:08.740 --> 00:28:10.600
aliens as they enter the screen.

00:28:11.380 --> 00:28:12.920
Sounds pretty standard, right?

00:28:13.560 --> 00:28:14.540
But. It'd be fun.

00:28:14.540 --> 00:28:19.000
But it comes with an incredibly complicated story.

00:28:19.260 --> 00:28:24.600
You see, when we last saw Paul and Vince, they had saved the colonel and were about to head

00:28:24.600 --> 00:28:28.640
for home in a special plane given to them by the general.

00:28:29.280 --> 00:28:34.460
But then while in flight over the ocean, the sky suddenly blackens.

00:28:34.620 --> 00:28:37.640
The ocean begins to churn and the plane goes spinning.

00:28:37.720 --> 00:28:40.440
A booming voice fills the cockpit.

00:28:40.440 --> 00:28:42.320
Hear me, warriors.

00:28:42.880 --> 00:28:46.780
Zhang Zip, the war dog, has enslaved the people of Earth.

00:28:47.040 --> 00:28:50.240
Only you can save us from his grip of evil.

00:28:51.020 --> 00:28:56.920
Caught in a time warp, hurtled thousands of years into the future, Paul and Vince know they

00:28:56.920 --> 00:29:00.700
have no choice but to meet this impossible challenge head on.

00:29:01.080 --> 00:29:03.640
After all, they are professionals.

00:29:04.200 --> 00:29:05.780
Dot, dot, dot.

00:29:06.340 --> 00:29:09.340
They are the Ikari Warriors.

00:29:09.340 --> 00:29:10.420
They said the name.

00:29:10.640 --> 00:29:16.860
And we've had some goofy stories and manuals before, but is this like the laziest story?

00:29:16.980 --> 00:29:18.600
I'd say maybe laziest, sure.

00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:20.580
But there have been more goofball.

00:29:20.580 --> 00:29:25.460
Oh, there's been more ridiculous. But this is like the laziest like, oh yeah, they were flying away and then someone attacked

00:29:25.460 --> 00:29:26.480
and they gotta go fight now.

00:29:26.680 --> 00:29:31.080
This is clearly just trying to get like an aliens thing going on because that movie is

00:29:31.080 --> 00:29:34.160
like taking off and now it's like, cool, let's make a game for you.

00:29:34.220 --> 00:29:36.900
Do you see the aliens influences in this game?

00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:40.520
I just think like, you know, just the idea of like aliens.

00:29:40.940 --> 00:29:42.160
Yeah. Any kind of aliens.

00:29:42.360 --> 00:29:44.940
Yeah. Marines taking down aliens too.

00:29:45.560 --> 00:29:46.620
I won't lie.

00:29:46.920 --> 00:29:50.120
Halfway through playing this game, I stopped and checked to make sure I was playing the

00:29:50.120 --> 00:29:54.120
right game. Just thinking back to the original Ikari Warriors, I was like, this can't be the sequel.

00:29:54.300 --> 00:29:55.920
Think about the way this game starts.

00:29:56.100 --> 00:29:57.660
There's no intro whatsoever.

00:29:57.720 --> 00:30:00.160
There's nothing about this like, you know, plain.

00:30:00.580 --> 00:30:01.460
There is an intro.

00:30:01.460 --> 00:30:02.420
Yes. And it is horrible.

00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:04.200
You have to wait. Oh, okay.

00:30:04.300 --> 00:30:08.640
Okay. That's good to know because I was going to say, Ikari Warriors 1 has an intro.

00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:13.040
You know, like even that one has like the, they actually did like some aspect ratio thing

00:30:13.040 --> 00:30:14.860
for it too to make it look like it was a movie.

00:30:15.040 --> 00:30:18.800
And the plane like crashes in the jungle and then you have to like start the game.

00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:22.000
So please, now that you've seen the intro, what happens in it?

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:28.940
It's more or less what you just described, but with three semi-moving pains.

00:30:29.360 --> 00:30:33.580
But is it clear if you didn't read the manual, would that have cleared it up and like, I think

00:30:33.580 --> 00:30:35.100
I'm going into the future right now.

00:30:35.260 --> 00:30:36.280
Does that make clear?

00:30:36.460 --> 00:30:42.600
There's obviously some supernatural thing happening to the plane and then there's some guy talking

00:30:42.600 --> 00:30:44.620
to you and then you start playing the game.

00:30:44.620 --> 00:30:49.880
Like you could piece it together like you could watching like a foreign film and not

00:30:49.880 --> 00:30:53.740
really knowing the actual plot, but at least getting the gist of it.

00:30:53.920 --> 00:30:54.760
You know what I mean? Yes.

00:30:55.200 --> 00:30:58.280
You're missing a big detail about this, this intro too, is that.

00:30:58.300 --> 00:31:03.500
It has the worst text crawl speed of anything I've ever seen before.

00:31:03.780 --> 00:31:07.840
It is painful. It's almost like more than a second per letter that has to appear.

00:31:08.040 --> 00:31:09.360
And you know why?

00:31:09.380 --> 00:31:10.640
It's because it's Morse code.

00:31:11.060 --> 00:31:12.820
The beeps that are, I'm not kidding.

00:31:12.820 --> 00:31:15.000
The beeps that are appearing are Morse code.

00:31:15.620 --> 00:31:19.860
Like, so it just plays Morse code of the whole story it's telling you.

00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:21.300
It's four minutes long.

00:31:22.540 --> 00:31:24.500
But you have the option to hit like empty, right?

00:31:24.500 --> 00:31:25.500
You do. You can stop it.

00:31:25.500 --> 00:31:29.780
Maybe that's why they didn't make it like automatic, like that you should start with

00:31:29.780 --> 00:31:36.180
that. Because as anybody who's ever played Ikario Warriors 2, Victory Road will tell you, you

00:31:36.180 --> 00:31:41.680
will die very quickly the first time you ever boot up this game because I would describe

00:31:41.680 --> 00:31:45.680
the controls of this game fever dream levels of failure.

00:31:46.100 --> 00:31:50.260
You know? And what I mean by that is when you're in a dream and all of a sudden you have to punch

00:31:50.260 --> 00:31:52.000
something. Flip a light?

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:53.240
Yeah. Flip a light switch.

00:31:53.620 --> 00:31:56.420
Anything, actually. Not even just combat in this game.

00:31:56.480 --> 00:32:00.580
Just when you're trying to do anything in this game, including walking, I just feel like

00:32:00.580 --> 00:32:04.020
you have very little control over what is going on.

00:32:04.220 --> 00:32:12.660
And I think that this game shocked me the first time I played it because I started, I

00:32:12.660 --> 00:32:13.760
died very quickly.

00:32:13.760 --> 00:32:14.940
I started again.

00:32:14.940 --> 00:32:16.760
