00:32:22.540 --> 00:32:23.520
that's coming at you.

00:32:23.520 --> 00:32:28.340
I found it was, so what was interesting about it is I appreciate that it tried to kind of

00:32:28.340 --> 00:32:31.440
fix a problem with the original where it allowed you to strafe.

00:32:31.800 --> 00:32:35.060
So you don't, you don't have to turn when you, when you, when you want to go left and

00:32:35.060 --> 00:32:42.340
turn when you want to go right. The strafing, you hold the fire button to strafe, which just makes it like almost, they

00:32:42.340 --> 00:32:43.780
created the opposite problem.

00:32:43.900 --> 00:32:47.820
Now it's really, really difficult to turn and things come up on your, on your sides.

00:32:47.820 --> 00:32:55.520
It, so I had completely forgotten almost all of my gameplay experience from Ikari Warriors

00:32:55.520 --> 00:32:56.420
when I played.

00:32:56.540 --> 00:33:01.420
You didn't go back. Then I, then I went back after, after like, you know, the first five minutes of playing

00:33:01.420 --> 00:33:03.840
this game, like I need to see what I'm even working with here.

00:33:03.900 --> 00:33:06.740
Like what should I have remembered of how to play this game?

00:33:06.860 --> 00:33:12.580
And yeah, I did realize that, okay, that they've added this new control feature that allows

00:33:12.580 --> 00:33:18.220
you to mimic the arcade game a little bit better, but at what cost?

00:33:18.620 --> 00:33:25.520
Yeah. The, even if you're not trying to fire, if you're just trying to turn around, your character

00:33:25.520 --> 00:33:27.340
makes like a semi-circle.

00:33:27.600 --> 00:33:29.400
Yeah. He doesn't pivot on the spot.

00:33:30.380 --> 00:33:36.740
It's like this really weird mix of sludgy mechanics that creates this terrible experience.

00:33:38.560 --> 00:33:40.020
When I played, yeah, yeah.

00:33:40.100 --> 00:33:43.140
When I played Ikari Warriors 2, I said, hold on a minute.

00:33:43.280 --> 00:33:45.120
Like I, I must've died like six times in a minute.

00:33:45.280 --> 00:33:46.700
I said, hold on a minute.

00:33:47.860 --> 00:33:49.900
Ikari Warriors 1 wasn't this bad, right?

00:33:50.100 --> 00:33:53.540
And I went back and played it and I was like, okay, no, no, I remember this now.

00:33:53.660 --> 00:33:54.500
This is, this is kind of normal.

00:33:54.620 --> 00:33:59.920
And then, and then sure enough, I was like, nah, man, we just, we've come a long way in

00:33:59.920 --> 00:34:04.360
the NES. It's like, like when this, when that game came out, Ikari Warriors might've been like episode

00:34:04.360 --> 00:34:05.860
25. I don't even know.

