No, it's kind of like a one-hit KO kind of thing.

00:41:38.060 --> 00:41:41.020
I think I was doing for, like, bosses, too, and stuff like that.

00:41:41.260 --> 00:41:43.280
Oh. Yeah. Maybe I should have saved that.

00:41:43.460 --> 00:41:45.320
Well, maybe, but, like, how would you know?

00:41:45.640 --> 00:41:46.440
And also, what are you going to do?

00:41:46.660 --> 00:41:47.660
Not shoot?

00:41:47.860 --> 00:41:49.900
You're right. So, it's like, whatever.

00:41:50.160 --> 00:41:55.800
You know, all these things also don't appear to be, like, programmed to appear, like, at appropriate times, right?

00:41:55.800 --> 00:41:58.340
They're just kind of, like, littering the screen.

00:41:58.600 --> 00:42:02.280
Yeah. You know, so it's not like arrow power was, like, strategically placed.

00:42:02.700 --> 00:42:04.280
Yeah, usually they're...

00:42:05.560 --> 00:42:09.560
Before I get into what I think we're going to get into, which is, like, the shop mechanic,

00:42:09.760 --> 00:42:13.400
but I just want to go back to the boomerang one more time.

00:42:13.540 --> 00:42:24.440
Yep. And I don't know if it's just broken code or if they were trying to simulate something, but when I was shooting the boomerang,

00:42:24.560 --> 00:42:29.460
it seems that I could clear a full third of the screen without actually hitting an enemy.

00:42:30.260 --> 00:42:31.380
It was just, like...

00:42:31.380 --> 00:42:32.440
Like the hitbox is too large?

00:42:32.440 --> 00:42:39.720
The hitbox was a third of the screen, whereas the sprite was maybe, like, 30 pixels wide or something like that.

00:42:39.920 --> 00:42:41.460
Did you have the same experience, Joe?

00:42:41.460 --> 00:42:42.440
Yeah, something like that.

00:42:42.560 --> 00:42:48.020
I felt like sometimes I would just be aiming forward and the boomerang would just magnetize to whoever I...

00:42:48.020 --> 00:42:49.000
See, I didn't even see it.

00:42:49.140 --> 00:42:51.340
I didn't see the boomerang hit anything.

00:42:51.340 --> 00:42:53.840
It just would evaporate them next to it.

00:42:54.080 --> 00:42:55.880
I just thought I was really good at the game.

00:42:57.120 --> 00:42:58.320
But yeah, I felt the same...

00:42:58.320 --> 00:42:59.240
I felt, like, the same thing.

00:42:59.320 --> 00:43:01.620
I was, like, never sure. Like, I guess the boomerang is killing these things.

00:43:01.720 --> 00:43:03.080
I'm just never sure what's actually happening.

00:43:03.420 --> 00:43:09.420
And it's fine when something like that is reserved to, like, a thunder power thing where it just zaps all the enemies off the screen.

00:43:09.420 --> 00:43:10.760
Like, that's okay.

00:43:11.240 --> 00:43:16.040
It's another thing when, like, an item that you can just repeatedly use takes up half the screen.

00:43:16.160 --> 00:43:19.060
It's like, why even bother switching and stuff?

00:43:19.200 --> 00:43:27.040
But you do have the option to switch and buy things and collect money in this game because there's also the bar shop.

00:43:27.260 --> 00:43:31.920
Yeah. Which was exclusively, I think, added for the NES version.

00:43:31.920 --> 00:43:33.640
It wasn't in the arcade game.

00:43:34.060 --> 00:43:37.580
Just trying to jump on that RPG thing that's been going on recently.

00:43:38.000 --> 00:43:44.900
And I don't know. It just feels like it's completely not needed in this, like, clear arcade-style game.

00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:51.440
I'm not trying to, like, you know, like, just keep it to high score, even though I always say I don't care about that.

00:43:51.680 --> 00:43:54.320
Like, this is one of those elements where it's finally, like, I'm like, I don't know.

00:43:54.360 --> 00:43:56.440
What do I need to take on the next thing?

00:43:56.440 --> 00:44:00.140
I think that's, for me, that was, like, a matter of I was excited when I saw it.

00:44:00.200 --> 00:44:02.340
And then it was just I thought it was a cool thing.

00:44:02.340 --> 00:44:03.960
It would be great to have.

00:44:04.140 --> 00:44:06.680
And then it was just implemented into a really poor game.

00:44:06.860 --> 00:44:10.320
I think it's the way that you control, though, in this game.

00:44:10.320 --> 00:44:15.180
Because we saw this in Gun.Smoke, a similar, like, you can buy items.

00:44:15.180 --> 00:44:21.000
But I felt like in that one I knew what I needed to get done for, like, a particular situation or level.

00:44:21.200 --> 00:44:24.020
In this one it's like you have no idea what's coming next.

00:44:24.100 --> 00:44:30.980
And so it's like just, I don't know, give me, you know, I'll take the boomerang, I guess.

00:44:31.060 --> 00:44:35.780
You know, like what else could I really want out of what they're selling?

00:44:36.080 --> 00:44:40.020
The whole, what this is replacing is just drops.

00:44:40.320 --> 00:44:44.040
And this game already has drops where you just run and pick something up.

00:44:44.440 --> 00:44:50.560
But this is sort of like having, you're playing Time Crisis.

00:44:51.040 --> 00:44:59.160
And instead of, like, reloading, you have to play this weird mini game where you talk to somebody about how to reload.

00:44:59.460 --> 00:45:01.660
And then you go back into the action.

00:45:01.940 --> 00:45:05.140
Like, it's just completely unnecessary for the genre of the game.

00:45:05.140 --> 00:45:07.040
It's just completely tacked on.

00:45:07.560 --> 00:45:11.560
I like the, like, the art of these weird creatures in a bar.

00:45:11.820 --> 00:45:13.380
But that's the only thing about it.

00:45:13.380 --> 00:45:14.880
Yeah, for the shop element I do agree.

00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:22.040
Yeah. And I guess I was referring more to the, just the element of having, like, customizable or having, like, different items or whatever.

00:45:22.220 --> 00:45:23.380
The entire inventory system.

00:45:23.480 --> 00:45:24.460
Yeah, exactly. I see.

00:45:25.120 --> 00:45:28.120
And then there's the, um, the subscreen.

00:45:28.880 --> 00:45:33.780
Yeah. Which is just the, uh, UI of, like, hidden behind the select button.

00:45:33.960 --> 00:45:38.240
But I'm actually going to say that this is maybe the only thing I was like, oh, good job.

00:45:38.360 --> 00:45:44.500
Because it feels like a very efficiently, like, designed thing to see everything that you would need to see.

00:45:44.520 --> 00:45:45.560
The screen itself. Right.

00:45:45.560 --> 00:45:49.340
But when you use anything that's on the screen, like, half the time it's like, I didn't need that.

00:45:49.400 --> 00:45:53.800
Right. But it actually feels like every piece of information is communicated on that screen.

00:45:53.800 --> 00:45:57.620
Yeah. And it was easy to kind of get between the different, uh, segments that you need.

00:45:57.660 --> 00:46:00.920
Like, oh, here's your weapon, your A weapons and your B weapons and your items.

00:46:01.080 --> 00:46:02.400
They had a very good menu design.

00:46:02.480 --> 00:46:04.020
Yeah. Yes. And it's just funny because I could see.

00:46:04.020 --> 00:46:13.300
Great game. I could know because I could see them actually making the mistake of, like, specific, some items go up by your character and other items go in the item box.

00:46:13.300 --> 00:46:16.840
And, like, the weapons for player one are on player two's column.

00:46:17.060 --> 00:46:24.740
You know? Like, you can see those things happening because the rest of this game is so sloppy that it's amazing that they managed to make something that was easily digestible.

00:46:24.900 --> 00:46:35.520
I think that the manual actually, like, over-explains what you need to use the subscreen but doesn't quite flesh out, like, power-up items and weapons and stuff like that.

00:46:35.520 --> 00:46:48.900
What they should have done, since everything in this game seems to be, like, an extraneous feature, is add, like, some Resident Evil 4-style inventory management where you have to, like, each item is different size and you have to, like, rotate them and stuff.

00:46:49.020 --> 00:46:52.120
Like, I think that would be really cool if we're going to have, like, a shop.

00:46:52.300 --> 00:46:53.620
Sure. We also didn't have...

00:46:53.620 --> 00:46:55.620
Did we have an ammo thing here?

00:46:55.880 --> 00:46:58.320
Like... No. I think ammo was unlimited, right?

00:46:58.320 --> 00:47:02.500
So that would have been, like, a good reason to have a shop, too, if you have to buy ammo.

00:47:02.680 --> 00:47:10.080
But, you know, I guess they weren't counting on people being able to hit things when they need to because I certainly couldn't.

00:47:10.880 --> 00:47:15.500
All right. I think that's everything I wanted to talk about the gameplay of this game.

00:47:15.500 --> 00:47:17.060
Does anybody have any straight thoughts?

00:47:17.340 --> 00:47:18.560
I was a little...

00:47:18.560 --> 00:47:23.820
I mean, not that I could be more disappointed by anything because I didn't really like my baseline experience.

00:47:23.820 --> 00:47:28.520
But the bosses were all the same except for the last one.

00:47:29.220 --> 00:47:31.920
And... And they're all different than the arcade equivalents.

00:47:32.100 --> 00:47:33.960
Yeah. The arcade bosses look pretty good, actually.

00:47:34.480 --> 00:47:42.300
And it was basically just, like, here's a spider of some kind, I guess, or a scorpion.

00:47:42.520 --> 00:47:45.540
And then here's a scorpion with no arms.

00:47:45.540 --> 00:47:47.440
And here's a scorpion with longer arms.

00:47:47.460 --> 00:47:52.240
And then there's the main antagonist's brother at the very end.

00:47:52.240 --> 00:47:56.820
Like, well, I don't really understand what went into the boss design of this game.

00:47:57.240 --> 00:47:59.000
Did you get to the final boss?

00:47:59.160 --> 00:48:00.220
No. Did you?

00:48:00.380 --> 00:48:01.700
I didn't get to the final boss.

00:48:01.800 --> 00:48:02.920
I think it's, like, level three.

00:48:03.040 --> 00:48:04.660
And then I watched a video of the final boss.

00:48:05.440 --> 00:48:07.200
I did get to the final boss.

00:48:07.320 --> 00:48:09.260
And it was just the most...

00:48:09.260 --> 00:48:17.740
It was more frustrating than the rest of the game because it was just adding on every frustration at once.

00:48:18.120 --> 00:48:21.160
Got it. It was just like, here's everything the game has to offer all at once.

00:48:21.160 --> 00:48:23.700
Yeah. And apparently...

00:48:23.700 --> 00:48:26.040
Can you describe the final boss?

00:48:26.180 --> 00:48:27.640
Because apparently the final boss...

00:48:27.640 --> 00:48:30.960
I watched the arcade version and I thought, like, oh, that's really cool.

00:48:30.960 --> 00:48:35.880
It's like this green monster with tentacles and flies around the screen and stuff like that.

00:48:36.060 --> 00:48:36.860
Would it like that?

00:48:36.860 --> 00:48:39.600
In my mind's eye, it's a, like...

00:48:40.060 --> 00:48:42.780
It's sort of like a scary teddy bear.

00:48:43.120 --> 00:48:45.920
Okay. That sounds a lot different than what I've described to you.

00:48:45.920 --> 00:48:51.300
And he comes in and he's just like, hey, I'm Zang Zip's brother.

00:48:52.020 --> 00:48:53.200
He's a weird dude.

00:48:53.420 --> 00:48:55.000
And then he starts fighting you.

00:48:55.080 --> 00:48:56.620
And I didn't beat him.

00:48:56.960 --> 00:49:00.520
But, yeah, again, watching a video, as soon as he dies, it just says end.

00:49:01.020 --> 00:49:02.580
Right. Yeah. It doesn't even say end.

00:49:02.720 --> 00:49:03.660
It just goes to the credits.

00:49:03.860 --> 00:49:05.260
Credits and then end. Oh, does that end?

00:49:05.260 --> 00:49:07.460
Not as abrupt as some of our games, at least.

00:49:07.560 --> 00:49:10.920
They did give you, like, the, like, at least, like, a song or something.

00:49:10.920 --> 00:49:16.540
But you don't even beat the guy, the named main antagonist, Zang Zip or Zong Zorn.

00:49:16.800 --> 00:49:18.200
Like, you don't fight him.

00:49:18.200 --> 00:49:19.800
You fight his brother.

00:49:20.200 --> 00:49:22.460
That's crazy. Yeah, that's really weird.

00:49:22.560 --> 00:49:23.440
What was the... I don't know.

00:49:23.440 --> 00:49:24.600
I didn't even think of that. What was the decision?

00:49:24.600 --> 00:49:25.400
I have no idea.

00:49:25.720 --> 00:49:28.640
Yeah. I have no opinion on that because I didn't get that far.

00:49:28.720 --> 00:49:30.280
So I don't really know what to tell you.

00:49:30.540 --> 00:49:35.740
But also, speaking of the other bosses, there's the scorpion guy you're talking about.

00:49:36.060 --> 00:49:39.180
His arms extend out to, like, a certain point on the screen.

00:49:39.440 --> 00:49:42.960
Yeah, you just stay behind it. If you just don't pass a certain line, you cannot get hit.

00:49:42.980 --> 00:49:44.740
And you have a projectile weapon.

00:49:45.820 --> 00:49:47.680
You just can't lose that battle.

00:49:47.980 --> 00:49:49.860
Sounds great. Happens three times.

00:49:50.200 --> 00:49:56.560
Yeah. There's also some connective tissue here that everybody needs to understand that I withheld

00:49:56.560 --> 00:49:58.280
purposefully at the beginning of this show.

